The attached image illustrates Nano-11's ability to facilitate antigen transport and uptake by antigen-presenting cells (APCs) in draining lymph nodes. Panel A presents flow cytometry data showing the presence and phenotype (CD11c and MHCII expression) of OVA-positive cells in lymph nodes one and two days post-injection for different OVA formulations. Panel B quantifies the mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of OVA within these cells, indicating significantly enhanced OVA uptake per cell when combined with Nano-11 compared to soluble OVA or aluminum hydroxide. Panel C further demonstrates that Nano-11 notably increases the percentage of OVA-positive migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) in the draining lymph node, highlighting its role in effectively targeting antigen to these key immune cells for an improved adaptive immune response.